{
    "ID": "259",
    "Name": "Use of Hard-coded Password",
    "Abstraction": "Variant",
    "Structure": "Simple",
    "Status": "Draft",
    "Diagram": "/data/images/CWE-259-Diagram.png",
    "Description": "The product contains a hard-coded password, which it uses for its own inbound authentication or for outbound communication to external components.",
    "ExtendedDescription": "\n\nThere are two main variations of a hard-coded password:\n\n```\n\t\tInbound: the product contains an authentication mechanism that checks for a hard-coded password.\n\t\tOutbound: the product connects to another system or component, and it contains a hard-coded password for connecting to that component.\n```\n",
